From a Thought to a Working Platform: PlacementHub

As a student, one thing always bothered me.

Placement preparation wasn't difficult because resources didn't exist.
It was difficult because everything was scattered.

Job updates in one place.
Coding resources in another.
Aptitude materials somewhere else.
Guidance hidden across countless websites and groups.

I kept asking myself:

"Why isn't there a single place where students can find everything they need for placements?"

Instead of waiting for someone else to build it, I decided to explore the idea myself.

That's how PlacementHub was born.

Using creative problem-solving, curiosity, and the effective use of AI, I transformed a simple observation into a functional platform designed to make placement preparation more organized and accessible.

💡 What I learned from this project:

• Great ideas often come from everyday frustrations.
• AI is most powerful when used to solve real problems.
• Building starts with asking better questions.
• You don't need to know everything before you begin.

This project is more than just a platform.

It's proof that identifying a problem, thinking creatively, and leveraging the right tools can turn an idea into something real.

I'd love to hear your thoughts and feedback!

🔗 Project: https://amiable-site-creation.lovable.app 

